<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_WebworkSlick.xml                 UtinniPatches - WEBWORK_WEB_STRUCTURES_1
  ============================================================================
  The "commandable-adhesive slick/locked" mechanism webwork_kit_spec.md §3
  and the owner-and-nest sitting (§1a's mapping table, "commandable adhesive
  (slick vs locked)") both named and explicitly deferred: "a mechanical
  slick-vs-locked web state is deferred to the roster/web-Things work, noted
  here so it is not lost." This is that state, v1, built to what those two
  passes actually specified and no further.

  Same shape as this campaign's own RM_OllathrixVenom / RSW_ShokkBound
  hediffs (HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay + TendDuration): kit §3's
  own player-experience line, "a doctor can free them," is
  HediffCompProperties_TendDuration; "slick vs locked" is two escalating
  Moving-capacity stages rather than one flat penalty.

  RULED-pattern reuse, not a fresh invention: RM_Hediff_SunScald's own
  2026-09-11 ruling ("top stage CRIPPLES, never downs — no loot piñata")
  governs here too. A structure that could down a caught pawn outright
  would be a much bigger call than "adhesive slick" ever asked for, so the
  top stage caps Moving hard rather than setting it to (near-)zero outright
  the way a lethal bind might.

  Refreshed by RM_CompAdhesiveSlick (RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors) — see
  RUT_WebworkStructures.xml for the structure wiring (RUT_Webwork_Web, the
  sheet web, is the one of the three that carries it: a broad plane a pawn
  actually stands IN, not a thin anchor line or a plumbing gutter).

  ❓INVENTED: all severity numbers, expecting the same live-balance pass
  every other number in this kit's build carries.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_Webwork_Slick</defName>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <label>webbed-slick</label>
    <labelNoun>a web-slick coating</labelNoun>
    <description>Silk-sap fouls boots and fur alike, thickening with every second spent against it. Given time it goes from a nuisance to a real hold — a doctor's tend cuts it loose far faster than waiting it out.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.85, 0.78, 0.55)</defaultLabelColor>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <tendable>true</tendable>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-0.6</severityPerDay>
        <showHoursToRecover>true</showHoursToRecover>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_TendDuration">
        <severityPerDayTended>-2.4</severityPerDayTended>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>sticky</label>
        <minSeverity>0</minSeverity>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <postFactor>0.85</postFactor>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>slicked</label>
        <minSeverity>0.35</minSeverity>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <postFactor>0.45</postFactor>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>locked</label>
        <minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <setMax>0.08</setMax>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
